<%# locals: photo, fallback_char, badge: nil, badge_soft: false, badge_sale: false
    badge_sale is the gate on the sale red: a caller passes it only for a
    real discount or an active deal, never for sold or a seller's label. %>
<%# The one shared anatomy the card family actually has: the image slot.
    deals/_card and listings/_card carried this block byte-similar — same
    class family, same responsive widths — and only the badge text and its
    softness differ, so those are the locals. The card BODIES stay local:
    a deal leads with its discount, a listing with its meta row, and one
    body partial serving both would be the parameter soup the
    purchasable-row refutation warned about. %>
<%# alt stays empty: both callers wrap this slot in a link named by the title
    and print the title beside it, so a filled alt reads the title twice. %>
<div class="deal-card-img">
  <% if photo %>
    <%= responsive_image_tag photo, alt: "", widths: [360, 720], sizes: "(max-width: 768px) 50vw, 220px" %>
  <% else %>
    <div class="deal-card-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><%= fallback_char %></div>
  <% end %>
  <% if badge.present? %>
    <span class="deal-badge<%= " deal-badge--soft" if local_assigns[:badge_soft] %><%= " deal-badge--sale" if local_assigns[:badge_sale] %>"><%= badge %></span>
  <% end %>
</div>
